### Parklane Backend - runnable request collection
### VS Code: install "REST Client". IntelliJ: open and click Run.
### Everything here is also runnable from the generated docs at /docs.

@host = http://localhost:8000
@api = {{host}}/api
@device = Transformer
@index = 1

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- discovery

### Route index
GET {{api}}

### Health + database ping
GET {{api}}/health

### Generated OpenAPI schema (Swagger UI is at /docs, ReDoc at /redoc)
GET {{host}}/openapi.json

### Every collection in Atal with its document count
GET {{api}}/collections

### Only this device's collections
GET {{api}}/collections?deviceType={{device}}


### ---------------------------------------------------------------- catalogue

### All 28 device types
GET {{api}}/devices/catalogue

### One type with its full tag list (names, kind, min/max)
GET {{api}}/devices/catalogue/{{device}}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------ devices

### Registered devices
GET {{api}}/devices

### Filter by category
GET {{api}}/devices?category=Electrical

### Register a device up front (optional - a POST reading does it automatically)
POST {{api}}/devices
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "deviceType": "Transformer",
  "index": 2,
  "location": "Substation B",
  "description": "Second 11kV/415V transformer"
}

### One device with its collections and document counts
GET {{api}}/devices/{{device}}/{{index}}

### Update device metadata
PATCH {{api}}/devices/{{device}}/{{index}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "location": "Substation A",
  "status": "active"
}

### Unregister, keeping the readings
DELETE {{api}}/devices/{{device}}/2

### Unregister and drop its collections
DELETE {{api}}/devices/{{device}}/2?dropCollections=true


### ------------------------------------------------------- readings :: create

### Create one reading - creates transformer_1_instant if it does not exist
POST {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/instant
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "timestamp": "2026-03-15T10:00:00Z",
  "tags": {
    "Voltage": 10476,
    "Current": 912,
    "Frequency": 50,
    "Power": 2253,
    "kWh": 262950628,
    "Temperature": 37,
    "alarms": 0,
    "Trip_Status": 0
  }
}

### Batch insert - an array on the same route
POST {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/instant
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "timestamp": "2026-03-15T10:01:00Z", "tags": { "Voltage": 10480, "Current": 905 } },
  { "timestamp": "2026-03-15T10:02:00Z", "tags": { "Voltage": 10462, "Current": 918 } }
]

### Fully-qualified tag names from the BMS export are accepted and normalised
POST {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/instant
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "timestamp": "2026-03-15T10:03:00Z",
  "tags": { "Transformer Voltage": 10470, "Transformer_Current": 900 }
}

### A flat CSV-export row works too - it is folded into tags automatically
POST {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/instant
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "Timestamp": "2026-03-15T10:04:00Z",
  "Voltage": 10455,
  "Current": 921,
  "Frequency": 50
}

### Idempotent ingestion - re-posting the same timestamp updates in place
POST {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/instant/upsert
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "timestamp": "2026-03-15T10:05:00Z",
  "tags": { "Voltage": 10450, "Current": 925 }
}

### A device outside the catalogue works too (returns an UNKNOWN_DEVICE_TYPE warning)
POST {{api}}/readings/Chiller/1/instant
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tags": { "Supply_Temp": 6.8, "Return_Temp": 12.1, "Run_Status": 1 }
}


### --------------------------------------------------------- readings :: read

### List, newest first
GET {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/instant

### Paginated, oldest first
GET {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/instant?page=1&limit=25&sort=timestamp&order=asc

### Time window
GET {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/instant?from=2026-03-01&to=2026-04-01

### Only the fields you need
GET {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/instant?fields=timestamp,tags.Voltage&limit=50

### Exact tag match - every reading with a trip
GET {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/instant?tags.Trip_Status=1

### Range on a tag
GET {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/instant?tags.Voltage[gte]=10000&tags.Voltage[lte]=11000

### Only seeded data
GET {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/instant?source=seed

### Newest reading
GET {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/instant/latest

### min / max / avg / sum / last per tag over a window
GET {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/instant/stats?from=2026-03-01&to=2026-04-01

### One reading by id - paste an _id from a list response
GET {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/instant/000000000000000000000000


### ------------------------------------------------------- readings :: update

### Merge at tag level - other tags are untouched
PATCH {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/instant/000000000000000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tags": { "Voltage": 10500 }
}

### Replace the whole reading
PUT {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/instant/000000000000000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "timestamp": "2026-03-15T10:00:00Z",
  "tags": { "Voltage": 10500, "Current": 900, "Frequency": 50 }
}


### ------------------------------------------------------- readings :: delete

### One reading
DELETE {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/instant/000000000000000000000000

### A time range
DELETE {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/instant?from=2026-01-01&to=2026-02-01

### Everything in the collection - the filter-less form needs confirm=true
DELETE {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/instant?confirm=true

### Drop a collection outright
DELETE {{api}}/collections/transformer_1_instant?confirm=true


### ---------------------------------------------------- monthly and yearly

### Build transformer_1_monthly from transformer_1_instant
POST {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/rollup/monthly

### Build transformer_1_yearly
POST {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/rollup/yearly

### Reprocess one window only
POST {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/rollup/monthly?from=2026-01-01&to=2026-06-30

### Read the monthly tier
GET {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/monthly

### One specific month
GET {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/monthly?year=2026&month=3

### Read the yearly tier
GET {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/yearly?year=2026

### Monthly documents are writable too
POST {{api}}/readings/{{device}}/{{index}}/monthly
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "timestamp": "2026-02-01T00:00:00Z",
  "tags": { "kWh": { "count": 43200, "min": 0, "max": 998877, "avg": 501233.5 } }
}
